<interrogationes unitas="motus">

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what is a Motus and why does it not write to the insula on every event?
    <responsum symbolum="Motus mutare_motum motus_effundere" via="lib/motus.worklog.md">The
      mobile tier: state that changes on every event (pan, zoom,
      pointer capture, the pending stroke, an app's gesture) lives in a
      plain struct in memory, and only the quiet point writes it to the
      insula. Painting happens per event, writing happens IN QUIET:
      mutare_motum is the one gate for changes and never touches the
      insula; motus_effundere is the one quiet-time write (lint L4
      allows writes of the mobile fields only from its quies
      seat).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I change pan or zoom from an event handler so it gets saved later?
    <responsum symbolum="mutare_motum MotusMutator motus_quies motus_effundere dispensator_motus">Write
      a MotusMutator (vacuum fn(Motus*, vacuum* ctx)) that edits
      motus->pan or motus->zoom, and run it through
      mutare_motum(motus, fn, ctx, ev->tempus): it records the time and
      marks the Motus dirty. The dispensator then checks motus_quies
      with its own quies_ms on each event and calls motus_effundere,
      which writes pan_x, pan_y and zoom with insula_attributum_ponere
      (replacing, so a second flush does not double them) and clears
      the dirty flag when the write was accepted. Get the
      dispatcher's Motus with dispensator_motus.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I save an in-progress edit debounced, with its own quiet interval, and never lose it on quit?
    <responsum symbolum="motus_gestum_ponere mutare_gestum motus_gestus_quies motus_gestum_effundere dispensator_finire scriba_gestum_ponere">Attach
      the app's state once with motus_gestum_ponere(motus, status,
      effusor, ctx, quies_ms) (scriba uses SCRIBA_QUIES_MS, one
      second). Change it only through mutare_gestum, which does
      nothing if no gesture is attached. The dispatcher calls
      motus_gestum_effundere when motus_gestus_quies says the gesture's
      own interval has passed, and again in dispensator_finire. The
      gesture's dirty flag is separate from pan/zoom's: changing one
      never dirties the other.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why does my gesture stay dirty after motus_gestum_effundere?
    <responsum symbolum="motus_gestum_effundere MotusGestusEffusor" via="lib/vicus.c">The
      effusor returned FALSUM. A refusing effusor leaves the gesture
      dirty on purpose so the next quiet point tries again (and vicus
      refuses to switch away from an app whose dirty gesture will not
      flush, since the text would be lost). The call also returns
      FALSUM, and does nothing, when no gesture is attached, no
      effusor was given, or nothing changed since the last
      flush.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I flush the Motus from inside an action without losing the action's writer name?
    <responsum symbolum="motus_gestum_effundere motus_effundere insula_scriptorem_ponere" via="lib/motus.worklog.md">For
      the gesture, yes: motus_gestum_effundere sets the writer to
      "gestus" for the effusor and then restores the previous writer
      (fixed 2026-10-05, because scriba flushes on Esc and dd inside
      an action). motus_effundere does not: it writes as "motus" and
      then sets the writer to an empty chorda, so later writes in the
      same action are anonymous and owned attributes refuse them
      silently. Set the writer again after calling it. The
      dispatcher also calls motus_effundere itself when focus moves
      into another branch while pan/zoom is dirty.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I rely on the pending stroke in ictus_pendens being saved at quiet time?
    <responsum symbolum="motus_effundere motus_initiare">No.
      motus_effundere writes only pan_x, pan_y and zoom. The pending
      stroke (a Xar of Punctum created by motus_initiare) never reaches
      the insula; a finished stroke leaves through a document action,
      which goes into history. Capture and stroke are thrown away when
      vicus switches away from an app (xar_vacare on
      ictus_pendens).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I know which insula branch motus_effundere writes into?
    <responsum symbolum="motus_effundere insula_ramus_radix mutare_ramum">It
      takes the first one set: motus->ramus_intimus (the innermost
      focused branch the dispatcher found along the focus chain), else
      motus->ramus (the active branch the host set, for example the
      focused side in vicus), else insula_ramus_radix(repo). A branch
      counts as set when its repo is not NIHIL; motus_initiare zeroes
      both, so a standalone app writes to the root.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how does a component tell whether its branch has focus?
    <responsum symbolum="motus_ramus_focatus">Call
      motus_ramus_focatus(motus, ramus). It is VERUM when there is no
      Motus, when the branch is the root (empty via, an app on its
      own), or when motus->spatium equals the branch's via. The
      scriba, pictor, kalendarium, nomenclator, colloquia and
      admonitiones panes use it to decide whether to draw their focus
      indication.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
